ght).\n$$\n\nThe exact answer is\n\n$$\n3\\left(\\ln\\left(11\\right)-\\ln\\left(8\\right)\\right).\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186683242 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "55a0eaaf-8470-5260-abcc-1bda98163d43" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\left(\\ln\\left(7\\right)-\\ln\\left(5\\right)\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186683228}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "55a0eaaf-8470-5260-abcc-1bda98163d43" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\left(\\ln\\left(7\\right)-\\ln\\left(5\\right)\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186683228} :answer-field/id #uuid "10eb30fc-60c0-550a-9e0b-73315f651eaf" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186683213}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b8e6f16f-4e6e-54e3-ad91-b58eab9d4503" :question/problem "Evaluate exactly.\n\n$$\n\\int_{\\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}}^{\\ln{\\left(3 \\right)}} \\frac{6 e^{x}}{2 e^{x} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\n{{answer}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=2 e^{x} + 1$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(2 e^{x})\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nTransform both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}&\\Longrightarrow u=5\\\\x=\\ln{\\left(3 \\right)}&\\Longrightarrow u=7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{\\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}}^{\\ln{\\left(3 \\right)}} \\frac{6 e^{x}}{2 e^{x} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=3\\left(\\int_{5}^{7} \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEndpoint values: $e^{\\ln 2}=2,\\quad e^{\\ln 3}=3$.\n\nUse the integration rule:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\ln\\left|u\\right|+C.\n$$\n\nEvaluate the primitive and subtract lower from upper:\n\n$$\n3\\left(\\left[\\ln\\left|u\\right|\\right]_{5}^{7}\\right)=3\\left(\\left(\\ln{\\left(7 \\right)}\\right)-\\left(\\ln{\\left(5 \\right)}\\right)\\right).\n$$\n\nThe exact answer is\n\n$$\n3\\left(\\ln\\left(7\\right)-\\ln\\left(5\\right)\\right).\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186683251 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0fe06044-600f-535f-bed4-8ffc40f30073" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186683212}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0fe06044-600f-535f-bed4-8ffc40f30073" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186683212} :answer-field/id #uuid "c9c1f898-d92a-5cad-a8d1-08463d9e421e" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186683246}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e0fc7683-b8ed-592a-a25c-b785a2344d1a" :question/problem "Evaluate exactly.\n\n$$\n\\int_{0}^{1} 4 \\cdot 2^{x^{2}} x\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\n{{answer}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=x^{2}$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(2 x)\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nTransform both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=0&\\Longrightarrow u=0\\\\x=1&\\Longrightarrow u=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{0}^{1} 4 \\cdot 2^{x^{2}} x\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=2\\left(\\int_{0}^{1} 2^{u}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the integration rule:\n\n$$\n\\int 2^{u}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\frac{2^{u}}{\\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}}+C.\n$$\n\nEvaluate the primitive and subtract lower from upper:\n\n$$\n2\\left(\\left[\\frac{2^{u}}{\\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}}\\right]_{0}^{1}\\right)=2\\left(\\left(\\frac{2}{\\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{1}{\\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}}\\right)\\right).\n$$\n\nThe exact answer is\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{\\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}}.\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Definite Integrals"}]}
